[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40194"] :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}},$ $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}},$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{7}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{11}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{1\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{11}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(21[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+11[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140120/selection/93dbf45cc685a4fd31fe719f5bfe2059308640bdd8a91faf74dccea9e681c910" :answer/id #uuid "2a7904f4-5641-5eb7-b15f-974967f3dae0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140120/selection/edaa11a4172ebb9114cbb3cd5efc77148c77e8e938d85e3edf6471b694eaeaa5" :answer/id #uuid "2d736ac1-be96-5ff9-bd70-b9b2ec0445a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140120/selection/0b72124570587fa774e8de693770de530e3984895873031cc56799b172f22bcd" :answer/id #uuid "7fabdb13-e63a-5fac-8f0e-2adcc3b7c99b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140120/selection/1912a37c7e2687e4f871a096b15bb1d02c6645eba80ccd538f9e0b4b89129622" :answer/id #uuid "1882b753-ce87-5e1f-8c49-7f1045517fd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140120/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3111bcd7-e673-5843-b524-72001f890ad2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140120/selection/1912a37c7e2687e4f871a096b15bb1d02c6645eba80ccd538f9e0b4b89129622" :answer-field/choices ["q-140120/selection/93dbf45cc685a4fd31fe719f5bfe2059308640bdd8a91faf74dccea9e681c910" "q-140120/selection/edaa11a4172ebb9114cbb3cd5efc77148c77e8e938d85e3edf6471b694eaeaa5" "q-140120/selection/0b72124570587fa774e8de693770de530e3984895873031cc56799b172f22bcd" "q-140120/selection/1912a37c7e2687e4f871a096b15bb1d02c6645eba80ccd538f9e0b4b89129622"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140120" :question/id #uuid "5d784c99-ccfa-5cf1-aee8-af8e0a39bd18" :question/math-academy-id "q-140120" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}},$ $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}},$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{7\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{7\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{2}=3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{7\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2}{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+(-1)[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140120/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cae73a3-842e-5a1a-8774-35bba342845c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140120"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81472/selection/f45f329923c8e61f7031b5edecc0e5f5d611b4c59178c4c2a0444be93842b2e6" :answer/id #uuid "99b8e110-d675-5a88-9e2e-dc5d325e01d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81472/selection/4c35663e30d62e8d2b6654f67b9263fe99393b3004f705856db11baad963144a" :answer/id #uuid "84232768-408e-5e6c-8f79-61ccceb73140" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81472/selection/9ccb23a38bfa5545d85fc24b17e5be2eeaa0f7ef03b2b22c717b6785eaa5c57d" :answer/id #uuid "93f9c0f3-a652-5148-9ef1-32b5a0730a66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81472/selection/94e248177853882da6dba385f0b0a8936026d9872c1722d0461f87acc04703ac" :answer/id #uuid "ac92573d-f63f-5f41-9a03-f223047bd9e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81472/selection/6338bb5820bf28c3f69f712def7502dd7c9f355a6ee58f86360bd21a896ab598" :answer/id #uuid "8516c9e7-5f5e-547f-9678-281e8ff0dc70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81472/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cfcc758-2483-5389-8a77-c18a00e95769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81472/selection/94e248177853882da6dba385f0b0a8936026d9872c1722d0461f87acc04703ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-81472/selection/f45f329923c8e61f7031b5edecc0e5f5d611b4c59178c4c2a0444be93842b2e6" "q-81472/selection/4c35663e30d62e8d2b6654f67b9263fe99393b3004f705856db11baad963144a" "q-81472/selection/9ccb23a38bfa5545d85fc24b17e5be2eeaa0f7ef03b2b22c717b6785eaa5c57d" "q-81472/selection/94e248177853882da6dba385f0b0a8936026d9872c1722d0461f87acc04703ac" "q-81472/selection/6338bb5820bf28c3f69f712def7502dd7c9f355a6ee58f86360bd21a896ab598"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81472" :question/id #uuid "f5dbbef3-e100-51de-9e04-d411f861eff6" :question/math-academy-id "q-81472" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}},$ $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}},$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-12)\\cdot (-2)}{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-12)\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+(-12)\\cdot (-2)}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81472/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cae73a3-842e-5a1a-8774-35bba342845c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81472"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40616/selection/37c21b24e1fbb09c5b7baeaeaa6bc8677b99e0f21fbd8cde87ceb08d52e7a867" :answer/id #uuid "4ee825fb-2262-52ee-a613-729ebef83676" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40616/selection/ab672ef17a155ac2e9c86de8aaa9798b0e2cd2672a69487