c{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-4)+31\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+31\\cdot (-2)}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}w=-5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81593/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acb4bd03-9b89-5775-a700-e1f3ea9fa62e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81593"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81585/selection/6ba775f3862e094760e0411712ad1303014b112291927e83eb121755a0af4ce4" :answer/id #uuid "58726918-637a-5bd6-a352-b101207d8960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81585/selection/c16f7f3e4fb668806294a6a99b33272cce1bb80f34e521b3aef141966167d2cb" :answer/id #uuid "7e1f0fbf-4f9b-5ab4-a3b5-983524ba85b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81585/selection/e09940820cedef424fc4baec696247a584a3bf0c5dc6dd19445c1484de3d2f50" :answer/id #uuid "1c9f9ed7-5769-5250-8104-975d6bc3177a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81585/selection/732e2a571743e14fe384aaeda95616d13519e2350c7e41a4251f9c9e058c01c5" :answer/id #uuid "769f6b06-b69b-5d58-b2be-03e8456e931b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81585/selection/8b08dd80bf0be7098a2823522b8e82b1e8b5913fba1f03c149157a334a9d25bc" :answer/id #uuid "fb278d51-2145-5623-aeda-71f3a8cc2127" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "548b53e5-748f-53fe-892f-f85925e4347e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81585/selection/c16f7f3e4fb668806294a6a99b33272cce1bb80f34e521b3aef141966167d2cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-81585/selection/6ba775f3862e094760e0411712ad1303014b112291927e83eb121755a0af4ce4" "q-81585/selection/c16f7f3e4fb668806294a6a99b33272cce1bb80f34e521b3aef141966167d2cb" "q-81585/selection/e09940820cedef424fc4baec696247a584a3bf0c5dc6dd19445c1484de3d2f50" "q-81585/selection/732e2a571743e14fe384aaeda95616d13519e2350c7e41a4251f9c9e058c01c5" "q-81585/selection/8b08dd80bf0be7098a2823522b8e82b1e8b5913fba1f03c149157a334a9d25bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81585" :question/id #uuid "f29dd616-20ae-5ac6-8d0f-2176557e28bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81585" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-18)\\cdot (-2)+(-16)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4}{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-18)\\cdot (-3)+(-16)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-3)}{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}w=\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acb4bd03-9b89-5775-a700-e1f3ea9fa62e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40666"] :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{3\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}v=2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{3\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}w=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-82915/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "06a21957-878b-5e5f-b0cd-588057cab18d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82915/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "7275dc04-817d-58cf-9ea2-db78f97b35d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82915/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "36245817-c0b9-529e-a7f2-fb154a74b2b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82915/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "4186be12-2e1c-5b44-8691-8b57f89175bf