of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}},$ $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}},$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{3}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3+(-5)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=(-1)[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot 0}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+(-5)\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{3}=(-2)[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x$ coincides with the projection, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is zero $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-82915/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8eb07a32-45bd-5975-9f61-de6294d4895d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82915"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40615/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "032a1e0b-f5a5-5232-9b50-912d7e3593f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:an